+## Transparent Backgrounds
+
+Native alpha-channel transparency for OpenAI/Azure GPT Image models (`gpt-image-2.5-flare`, `gpt-image-2.5-sunburst`, `gpt-image-1`, `gpt-image-1.5`):
+
+```bash
+# Single sprite with transparent background
+${BUN_X} {baseDir}/scripts/main.ts --prompt "A knight sprite, isolated subject" --image sprite.png --provider openai --background transparent
+
+# Batch: per-task background overrides the base default
+# batch.json tasks accept "background": "transparent"|"opaque"|"auto"
+```
+
+Rules:
+
+- Request isolation in the prompt **and** pass `--background transparent` — the param alone does not guarantee clean silhouette edges.
+- Output must be png (default) or webp; jpeg cannot carry alpha and fails fast in validation.
+- `gpt-image-2` (non-2.5) and DALL·E models do not support transparency — use `opaque`/`auto` or switch models.
+- For transparent-by-default workflows, set `default_background: transparent` in EXTEND.md (CLI `--background` still wins per call).
 
